## Common Interview Questions

### Q1. What is Spring Boot?

Spring Boot is an extension of the Spring Framework that simplifies application development through auto-configuration, starter dependencies, and embedded servers.

### Q2. Why was Spring Boot introduced?

To reduce configuration complexity and speed up development.

### Q3. Does Spring Boot replace Spring Framework?

No.

Spring Boot is built on top of Spring Framework and uses Spring internally.

### Q4. What is the purpose of @SpringBootApplication?

It combines Configuration, Auto Configuration, and Component Scanning into a single annotation.

### Q5. What are Starter Dependencies?

Pre-configured dependency bundles that simplify project setup.

### Q6. What is Auto Configuration?

A mechanism that automatically configures Spring components based on project dependencies.

### Q7. What are the advantages of Embedded Tomcat?

* Easy deployment
* No external server setup
* Faster development
* Simplified configuration

---

## Summary

Spring Boot simplifies Java application development by reducing configuration effort, providing embedded servers, and enabling rapid application development.

It allows developers to focus on solving business problems rather than spending time on infrastructure setup.

Understanding Spring Boot fundamentals is essential before learning REST APIs, Spring Data JPA, Spring Security, and Microservices.

